            {"heading": "What Is Personal Bias?",
             "body": "A bias is a leaning toward one way of seeing or deciding something, often without realizing it's happening. Personal bias in money decisions means your brain has a built-in shortcut that affects how you spend, save, or think about money, separate from the actual facts of the situation. Bias isn't the same as being wrong on purpose. It's automatic. You can be a smart, careful person and still have money biases running in the background, because biases are less about intelligence and more about mental shortcuts your brain uses to make fast decisions in a world with too much information to fully weigh every time."},
